+`src/errors.ts` has the errors the service throws (`ValidationError`, `NotFoundError`, `ConflictError`, `RestoreExpiredError`); the handler maps them to 400, 404, 409 and 410 with a body of `{ error, message }`.
 
 ## Routes
 
@@ -16,8 +16,14 @@ The projects part of our internal tracker: an in-memory store, the rules around
 | `GET /projects` | 200 `{ projects }`, in creation order |
 | `GET /projects/:id` | 200 `{ project }` |
 | `PATCH /projects/:id` with `{ name }` | 200 `{ project }` |
-| `DELETE /projects/:id` | 204, and the project is gone |
+| `DELETE /projects/:id` | 204; the project is soft-deleted (see below) |
+| `POST /projects/:id/restore` | 200 `{ project }` |
+| `GET /projects?includeDeleted=true` | admins only: deleted projects are listed too, anyone else gets 403 |
 
 A request is `{ method, path, query?, body?, user? }` and `user` is `{ id, role }` with `role` either `"admin"` or `"member"`. A response is `{ status, body? }`.
 
 Time and ids come from `deps` (`now()`, `newId()`) so tests can control them.
+
+## Soft delete
+
+Deleting a project sets its `deletedAt` to the service clock's `now()`. A deleted project is missing for `get`, `rename`, `list` and the repository's `findById`/`findAll`, unless `includeDeleted: true` is passed, and it no longer holds its name. `restore` brings it back within 30 days of the deletion (`RESTORE_WINDOW_MS`); a second deletion restarts the 30 days.
